<Base lang="en" title="About"><article class="prose"><p class="label">About</p><h1>Schlaflied, a room by Syna.</h1><p>A public space where writing, learning, AI, open source, and traces of a life share the same desk. None of these need to justify the others, and none is reduced to a professional label.</p><p>The site lives in Chinese and English side by side. The languages will not always map one-to-one: originals, translations, introductions, and project notes will arrive in the language that suits them.</p><p>I'm Syna, also known as Schlaflied. I hold a Master of Professional Education and a BCom in Human Resources. I'm based in Ontario, Canada, currently job-hunting in Instructional Design / Learning Experience Design, and treating career-ops — an open-source job-search tool — as a real practice ground: from scoring logic to jurisdiction-compliance detection, I try to see designs through to something that actually ships. Chinese is the language I write in natively; English is my working language. This site is where both keep growing, side by side.</p><aside class="note about-excerpt"><strong>A note to whoever's reading this</strong><p>I've always believed years of employment aren't the same as ability — those years only ever hand you a title, and the moment you leave that company, the title disappears. What you keep is only the ability you actually built. Open source gave me another path. I don't have a CS degree, but the architecture I designed, and every issue I raised, became infrastructure that changed tens of thousands of users. Real self-worth was never handed to me by a degree or a job title — it came from what I built with my own hands, piece by piece.</p></aside><div class="about-contact"><p class="label">Contact</p><ContactRow lang="en" /></div></article></Base>

